description: Regras globais do boilerplate (stack, escopo, commits)
alwaysApply: true
---

# Global

- Stack: Next 16, Drizzle, NextAuth Credentials, DDD-lite + Ports & Adapters.
- Dependency flow: `presentation → application → domain ← infrastructure`.
- Use cases hold business rules; Route Handlers and Server Actions only orchestrate.
- Minimize diff scope — no drive-by refactors or unrequested features.
- Match existing naming, types, and factory patterns in sibling modules.
- Commits: Conventional Commits (`feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`).
- Quality gate: `make check` before PR; never push directly to `main` (branch protection).
- Deep context: `AGENTS.md`, `docs/agents/`, module READMEs under `src/modules/*/`.
- If `PROJECT.md` exists (derived product), read it for business scope before feature work.
